{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey maximum security deposit","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit (including any pet deposit) larger than one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly increase in the deposit may not exceed 10 percent of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; yearly increase max 10% of current deposit","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in New Jersey; at lease inception the landlord may also require the first month's rent, for a total of no more than two and one-half times monthly rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rentals"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and double-damages remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends, the landlord must return the security deposit plus interest earned, less lawful deductions, and send an itemized list of deductions by registered or certified mail.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; if a tenant breaks the lease without legal cause, the 30 days runs from re-rental or lease expiration, whichever is first.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rentals"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees; a displaced tenant gets the deposit within 5 business days of displacement.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit account, trust and interest rules","requirement":"A landlord must hold deposit money in trust and deposit it in an insured New Jersey bank or savings institution in an interest-bearing account; interest belongs to the tenant and is paid at renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 after written notice.","key_value":"10 or more units: money market or variable-rate account option; interest to tenant annually","coverage_conditions":"Landlords receiving security deposit money for residential units; those with 10 or more units may instead invest in an insured New Jersey money market fund maturing in one year or less.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Turns on number of units held, not owner type"},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental, meaning a term of not more than 125 consecutive days for residential purposes by a person with a permanent residence elsewhere.","penalty":"If the landlord fails to give required notice or pay interest, the tenant may apply the deposit plus interest at 7% per annum to rent after written notice; no further deposit may then be demanded.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"A landlord or designee who receives security deposit money for ten or less units must deposit that money in an insured bank or savings and loan association located in New Jersey in an interest-bearing account at the current interest rate at the time of deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days after termination and notify the tenant in writing within 3 business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a residential lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence; public housing tenants must follow applicable public housing regulations.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential leases terminated under the Safe Housing Act"},"exemptions":"Does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
